WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.330
- On this Wednesday Checkup,
I want to talk about

00:00:02.330 --> 00:00:05.000
the two urgent care doctors
that are making headlines

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:07.829
for their controversial
statements regarding COVID-19.

00:00:07.829 --> 00:00:10.579
(dramatic music)

00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:15.940
This all started on April 22
when two doctors Dan Erickson

00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:18.210
and Artin Massihi called
a press conference

00:00:18.210 --> 00:00:20.400
to discuss their thoughts on COVID-19

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:22.150
and the re-opening of America

00:00:22.150 --> 00:00:24.430
based on the five thousand
patients they tested

00:00:24.430 --> 00:00:25.710
in their Urgent Care centers.

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:28.330
The main takeaways from the
press conference are as follows:

00:00:28.330 --> 00:00:31.860
One, the government is horribly
mishandling this situation

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:34.190
by ignoring the science and only focusing

00:00:34.190 --> 00:00:35.520
on controlling the public.

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:38.550
Two, way more people
are sick with COVID-19

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:39.750
than is currently reported.

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:43.270
Three, the fatality rate
of COVID-19 is much lower

00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:46.020
than currently being reported
and it's similar to the flu.

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:48.920
And finally four, that
America should re-open now

00:00:48.920 --> 00:00:50.610
because the harms of keeping it closed

00:00:50.610 --> 00:00:52.120
much outweigh the benefits.

00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:54.200
In the days following
their press conference,

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:56.350
they received nationwide attention.

00:00:56.350 --> 00:00:58.980
Mostly because their
recommendations and opinions were

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:02.890
in stark contrast with the
medical community and the CDC.

00:01:02.890 --> 00:01:04.840
Also the video of the press conference

00:01:04.840 --> 00:01:07.470
became increasingly
popular on social media

00:01:07.470 --> 00:01:10.670
where it picked up over five
million views on YouTube.

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:13.110
And it received retweets
from popular figures

00:01:13.110 --> 00:01:15.790
like Elon Musk who supported the doctors.

00:01:15.790 --> 00:01:19.370
Fast Forward to April 27th
and YouTube has now taken

00:01:19.370 --> 00:01:20.800
the video down stating

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:22.920
that it's broken community guidelines,

00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:25.210
basically saying there's a
lot of misinformation in it.

00:01:25.210 --> 00:01:27.130
And there's been a
joint statement released

00:01:27.130 --> 00:01:29.087
by the American College
of Emergency Physicians

00:01:29.087 --> 00:01:32.180
and the American Academy
of Emergency Medicine.

00:01:32.180 --> 00:01:33.130
Let me read that statement.

00:01:33.130 --> 00:01:37.490
The AACP and AAEM jointly
and emphatically condemn

00:01:37.490 --> 00:01:40.917
the recent opinions released
by Dr Erickson and Dr Massihi.

00:01:40.917 --> 00:01:43.687
"These reckless and untested
musings do not speak

00:01:43.687 --> 00:01:46.037
"for medical society and are inconsistent

00:01:46.037 --> 00:01:49.517
"with current science and
epidemiology regarding COVID-19.

00:01:49.517 --> 00:01:51.767
"As owners of local urgent care clinics,

00:01:51.767 --> 00:01:54.677
"it appears these two
individuals are releasing biased,

00:01:54.677 --> 00:01:58.407
"non-peer reviewed data to
advance their personal financial

00:01:58.407 --> 00:02:00.910
"interests without regard
for the public's health."

00:02:00.910 --> 00:02:02.740
I completely agree with these statements

00:02:02.740 --> 00:02:04.310
because these individuals presented

00:02:04.310 --> 00:02:07.260
so much misinformation that
it's further gonna confuse

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:08.170
the general public.

00:02:08.170 --> 00:02:10.610
Let me explain why the information
these doctors presented

00:02:10.610 --> 00:02:12.480
is just not scientifically accurate.

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:15.310
Look, the fact that they
tested 5,000 patients

00:02:15.310 --> 00:02:17.680
in their Urgent Care centers and 6%

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:21.100
of them tested positive for
COVID-19 makes a lot of sense.

00:02:21.100 --> 00:02:22.980
And it's actually probably accurate.

00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:25.990
But what's not accurate and
what doesn't make sense is

00:02:25.990 --> 00:02:29.980
to then take 6%, that number
and assume that if you test

00:02:29.980 --> 00:02:32.330
all of New York State
and all of California,

00:02:32.330 --> 00:02:35.390
then 6% of those people
will also test positive.

00:02:35.390 --> 00:02:37.240
That's just not how statistics work.

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:39.390
The people that go to
an Urgent Care center

00:02:39.390 --> 00:02:41.110
are more likely to test positive

00:02:41.110 --> 00:02:42.480
because they're showing symptoms,

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:44.710
because they likely had
exposure to COVID-19,

00:02:44.710 --> 00:02:45.780
that's why they're there.

00:02:45.780 --> 00:02:48.740
In general when you're testing
a preselected population

00:02:48.740 --> 00:02:50.530
like that, you're gonna
have higher numbers.

00:02:50.530 --> 00:02:53.640
It's like assuming that if
you go to Southern California

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:56.550
and gather the weather data,
you can then extrapolate it

00:02:56.550 --> 00:02:58.490
and assume that the weather
is the same in New York.

00:02:58.490 --> 00:03:02.300
And then with the incorrect
assumption that 6%

00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:04.970
of the general public
must be COVID positive,

00:03:04.970 --> 00:03:07.249
they go on to calculate a fatality rate

00:03:07.249 --> 00:03:08.880
that's similar to the flu.

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:11.230
Let me go ahead and explain
to you how we calculate

00:03:11.230 --> 00:03:12.710
a death rate so it all makes sense.

00:03:12.710 --> 00:03:15.920
First we take all the people
who've died with COVID-19

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:18.500
and we divide that
number by all the people

00:03:18.500 --> 00:03:20.150
who've been infected by COVID-19.

00:03:20.150 --> 00:03:21.190
Let's run an example here.

00:03:21.190 --> 00:03:23.370
If 10 people have died of COVID-19

00:03:23.370 --> 00:03:24.960
and 1000 have been infected,

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:27.510
you divide 10 by 1000 and you get 1%.

00:03:27.510 --> 00:03:29.100
It makes a 1% death rate.

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:32.680
Now if you incorrectly
assume that way more people

00:03:32.680 --> 00:03:34.870
have had COVID-19 than is true,

00:03:34.870 --> 00:03:37.530
you can artificially
lower this death rate.

00:03:37.530 --> 00:03:39.650
My second issue is let's go ahead

00:03:39.650 --> 00:03:42.180
and assume there calculations are correct.

00:03:42.180 --> 00:03:43.013
They're not.

00:03:43.013 --> 00:03:45.960
It doesn't change the fact
that COVID-19 is still

00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:47.630
much more dangerous than the flu.

00:03:47.630 --> 00:03:51.860
Reason being that COVID-19
spreads at a two to three times

00:03:51.860 --> 00:03:53.440
faster rate than the flu.

00:03:53.440 --> 00:03:56.550
Which means that it can
overwhelm our hospital systems

00:03:56.550 --> 00:03:57.750
in the blink of an eye.

00:03:57.750 --> 00:03:59.350
In fact, that's what the purpose

00:03:59.350 --> 00:04:00.780
of all these lock downs were.

00:04:00.780 --> 00:04:03.040
To ease the strain on our hospital systems

00:04:03.040 --> 00:04:04.960
so we can continue taking care of patients

00:04:04.960 --> 00:04:07.000
that are not only suffering with COVID,

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:09.090
but with all the other
medical ailments out there.

00:04:09.090 --> 00:04:10.820
If you have been in a car accident,

00:04:10.820 --> 00:04:12.040
there would have been no one to help you.

00:04:12.040 --> 00:04:13.270
If you call for a heart attack,

00:04:13.270 --> 00:04:14.550
there would have been no one to help you.

00:04:14.550 --> 00:04:18.290
We must also remember that for
the flu, we have a vaccine.

00:04:18.290 --> 00:04:20.120
We have an FDA approved treatment.

00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:22.860
So by maintaining the lockdown
for slightly longer period

00:04:22.860 --> 00:04:26.090
of time, we're buying time
in order to get there.

00:04:26.090 --> 00:04:28.990
To get the vaccine and to get
the treatments authorized.

00:04:28.990 --> 00:04:32.200
These are all the reasons why
I've been consistently saying

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:34.880
on my YouTube channel, to
my patients, on television,

00:04:34.880 --> 00:04:38.590
that while COVID-19 looks
similar to the flu, it's a virus,

00:04:38.590 --> 00:04:41.430
upper respiratory symptoms,
they are not the same.

00:04:41.430 --> 00:04:44.910
They're fundamentally different
in that COVID-19 spreads

00:04:44.910 --> 00:04:47.600
so quickly and puts
such a tremendous strain

00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:49.690
on our health care system,
that it can break it.

00:04:49.690 --> 00:04:53.740
In fact, I'd love for these
emergency medicine physicians

00:04:53.740 --> 00:04:56.130
who are no longer working
in emergency rooms

00:04:56.130 --> 00:04:59.370
to come to New York City
and talk to the ER doctors

00:04:59.370 --> 00:05:02.690
that are working on the front
lines to see how overwhelmed

00:05:02.690 --> 00:05:06.830
they were with this apparently
mild virus during it's peak.

00:05:06.830 --> 00:05:09.550
Let's move on to the topic
of re-opening America.

00:05:09.550 --> 00:05:11.880
These individuals are adamant

00:05:11.880 --> 00:05:14.400
about re-opening America, right now.

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:17.000
Because they're talking about
the negative consequences

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:19.060
that are happening as a
result of this lockdown.

00:05:19.060 --> 00:05:22.080
Social issues, like domestic
violence and child abuse.

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:23.790
Patients not being able to get care

00:05:23.790 --> 00:05:25.890
because they are worried
about getting sick with COVID.

00:05:25.890 --> 00:05:28.040
Routine procedures being re-scheduled.

00:05:28.040 --> 00:05:29.240
Economic harms.

00:05:29.240 --> 00:05:32.560
All of these negative
consequences are very true.

00:05:32.560 --> 00:05:34.492
And we need to take
them into consideration

00:05:34.492 --> 00:05:38.100
when we're weighing the benefits
versus harms of a lockdown.

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:40.880
The last thing we want to do is to rush

00:05:40.880 --> 00:05:43.098
to re-open America haphazardly

00:05:43.098 --> 00:05:47.080
and see a spike in the
resurgence of COVID-19 cases.

00:05:47.080 --> 00:05:49.400
Possibly destroying
our health care system,

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:52.060
potentially putting thousands
if not millions of lives

00:05:52.060 --> 00:05:54.030
at risk because they might not be able

00:05:54.030 --> 00:05:55.450
to get care at a hospital.

00:05:55.450 --> 00:05:57.960
Look we absolutely need
to start taking steps

00:05:57.960 --> 00:05:59.250
in re-opening America.

00:05:59.250 --> 00:06:01.049
If we continue this for much longer,

00:06:01.049 --> 00:06:02.980
it is gonna be limited benefits

00:06:02.980 --> 00:06:04.610
and more harms being added on.

00:06:04.610 --> 00:06:06.970
But the way we do this is strategically.

00:06:06.970 --> 00:06:08.980
We open certain areas first,

00:06:08.980 --> 00:06:11.960
and we continuously
gather information to see

00:06:11.960 --> 00:06:14.630
what impact we're having
on COVID-19 numbers.

00:06:14.630 --> 00:06:17.380
And then use that data
to gradually re-open

00:06:17.380 --> 00:06:22.360
the country slowly, carefully,
and most importantly, safely.

00:06:22.360 --> 00:06:25.030
At the end of the day, no one benefits

00:06:25.030 --> 00:06:26.860
from keeping America closed.

00:06:26.860 --> 00:06:29.480
In fact this whole theory of politicians

00:06:29.480 --> 00:06:32.020
keeping America closed
just to keep control

00:06:32.020 --> 00:06:34.460
over the general public is nonsensical.

00:06:34.460 --> 00:06:36.160
They're getting hurt by this too,

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:37.710
and so are their families.

00:06:37.710 --> 00:06:40.340
If you're gonna be a public
facing medical professional

00:06:40.340 --> 00:06:42.800
that goes on to talk
about COVID-19 and say

00:06:42.800 --> 00:06:44.480
that you're talking about science.

00:06:44.480 --> 00:06:47.510
At least do it accurately, and
keep the politics out of it.

00:06:47.510 --> 00:06:48.810
These doctors aren't the first

00:06:48.810 --> 00:06:51.320
to be spreading
misinformation about COVID-19.

00:06:51.320 --> 00:06:53.630
So are politicians and so is the media.

00:06:53.630 --> 00:06:54.930
Click here for those videos

00:06:54.930 --> 00:06:57.515
and as always stay happy and healthy.

00:06:57.515 --> 00:07:00.348
(dramatic music)

